    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_261dcc41dde8219998421fa09c23ea88205df759d7b577adc1ab222a6e243eb0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source separates logical validity from numerical sensitivity: the full product Δ_K²g_K(0) must satisfy the Lehmer criterion, but after that certification the Taylor expansion of λ_K shows that -Δ_K²/8 fixes the leading scale, explaining why coarse yet upward-safe interaction bounds can still yield a sharp near-zero lower bound.",
