      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d0bbb4e83c11793527741c59ec2939ed70a2c2656f15e833ad30400c0ae38ebd",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source turns a computationally selected close pair into a lower bound for Λ through a staged certificate: the all-other-zero interaction is partitioned into a local window, a finite distant-index block, and an infinite outer tail; separately justified upper bounds are recombined to verify the Lehmer threshold, and monotonicity then converts the interaction enclosure into the stated phase-boundary bound.",
